Don't you think that {mi ze'e pu prami do} could mean either {mi ze'e pu su=
'oroi prami do} (=3D"I have always loved you at least one time") or {mi ze'=
e pu roroi prami do} (=3D"I have always loved you at every time" (whatever =
"times" refers to here)) or {mi ze'e pu ru'i prami do} (=3D"I have always l=
oved you continuously") etc?
In most contexts I think the latter is the most plausible interpretation of=
 bare {ze'e pu}, don't you think?
{mi roroi prami do} could for example means {mi pu ze'u roroi ca ze'i pu pr=
ami do} (=3D"there was a time in the past when I at every occasion had love=
d you for a short time").
See also CLL 10.9.
mu'omi'e seb

